row(".round / .chamfer / short edges near SolidCraft's size floor (edge or arc shorter than about 1e-5 mm): valid inputs refused with the wrong cause", 'refused',
  `${cmd('round3')} + ${cmd('round3b')} Exact threshold, 10-wide plate with the two bottom corners rounded r each (flat = 10-2r left): r=4.9 / 4.99 / 4.999 / 4.9999 / 4.99999 (flat 2e-1 .. 2e-5) all BUILD and match brep-rs and the closed form (worst ${e(mx(bandPair, 'dVolExact'))}); flat 1e-5, 5e-6, 3e-6 and r=4.999999 (2e-6) are REFUSED although OCCT and brep-rs build them (e.g. ${n6(R('band-round-pair-flat0.00001').brep.volume)}). One corner on a 40x30 plate: r=1e-5 builds (volume off by 6.7e-4 mm3 absolute, 5.6e-8 relative, above the 1e-9 planar bar: the truck integration error on a tiny face; bbox exact), r=5e-6, 3e-6, 2e-6, 1e-6 REFUSED. Chamfer: d=1e-3 builds exactly, d=1e-5 builds with the same 5.6e-8 volume error, d=5e-6, 3e-6, 2e-6, 1e-6 REFUSED; chamfer leaving 1e-4 of the 30 edge builds, leaving 1e-5, 5e-6, 3e-6, 1e-6 REFUSED. So SolidCraft refuses any edge or arc shorter than about 1e-5 mm (a tolerance floor) and every sentence names the wrong thing: '${sentenceOf('round-pair-r4.999999')}' (the loop is closed), '${sentenceOf('round-single-r0.000001')}' (nothing is collinear), 'zero-length line' (the edge is 2e-6 long, not zero). Safe (no solid) but misleading.`,
  [eng(sentenceOf('round-pair-r4.999999'), 'Corners 1 and 2 are rounded so nearly to the limit that the straight piece between them is under 0.00001 mm; use a smaller radius.'), eng(sentenceOf('round-single-r0.000001'), 'A radius of 0.000001 is smaller than the 3D engine can build (about 0.00001 mm); use a larger radius or leave the corner sharp.'), eng(sentenceOf('chamfer-near-ceiling-d29.999999'), 'This chamfer leaves under 0.00001 mm of the edge; use a smaller distance.')].join(' | '));
