row("tessellate(sketch): sketch to polyline points (viewport / overlay only; not used by the SolidCraft build)", 'unsupported',
  `${cmd('2d')} Not mapped to SolidCraft at all (the build uses exact arcs, previous row), so it cannot be 'supported' for building or measuring. Measured accuracy as a standalone polyline, by shoelace area on the polyline vs exact: circle across 10 (${tm.samples} samples): area error ${e(tm.areaRel)} (= 1 - sin(2pi/48)/(2pi/48) = ${e(tm.expectedAreaRelFor48gon)}, i.e. ten times the 3e-4 curved bar; vertices on the true circle to ${e(tm.maxRadialError)}); semicircle bulge on a square: ${tb.samples} samples, area error ${e(tb.areaRel)}; 40x30 with four r5 rounds via outlineOf: ${tr.viaOutlineOf.samples} points (${tr.samplesPerCornerArc} per 90-degree arc), area error ${e(tr.viaOutlineOf.areaRel)}. IMPORTANT for callers: tessellate(sketch) alone IGNORES rounds and chamfers (a rounded 40x30 returns the sharp 4 corners, area 1200 vs exact ${n6(tr.viaOutlineOf.areaExact)}); only tessellate(outlineOf-result) is the rounded outline. So a polyline must never be used to measure a sketch against the 3e-4 bar; use the exact arcs.`);

